msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:1
msgid "Build Status"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:3
msgid ""
"This module provides a complete implementation of the WebSocket protocols"
" that can be hooked up to any I/O stream. It aims to simplify things by "
"decoupling the protocol details from the I/O layer, such that users only "
"need to implement code to stream data in and out of it without needing to"
" know anything about how the protocol actually works. Think of it as a "
"complete WebSocket system with pluggable I/O."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:10
msgid ""
"Due to this design, you get a lot of things for free. In particular, if "
"you hook this module up to some I/O object, it will do all of this for "
"you:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:13
msgid "Select the correct server-side driver to talk to the client"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:14
msgid "Generate and send both server- and client-side handshakes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:15
msgid "Recognize when the handshake phase completes and the WS protocol begins"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:16
msgid "Negotiate subprotocol selection based on `Sec-WebSocket-Protocol`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:17
msgid ""
"Negotiate and use extensions via the [websocket-"
"extensions](https://github.com/faye/websocket-extensions-node) module"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:20
msgid "Buffer sent messages until the handshake process is finished"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:21
msgid "Deal with proxies that defer delivery of the draft-76 handshake body"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:22
msgid "Notify you when the socket is open and closed and when messages arrive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:23
msgid "Recombine fragmented messages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:24
msgid "Dispatch text, binary, ping, pong and close frames"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:25
msgid "Manage the socket-closing handshake process"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:26
msgid "Automatically reply to ping frames with a matching pong"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:27
msgid "Apply masking to messages sent by the client"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:29
msgid ""
"This library was originally extracted from the "
"[Faye](http://faye.jcoglan.com) project but now aims to provide simple "
"WebSocket support for any Node-based project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:34
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:41
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:43
msgid ""
"This module provides protocol drivers that have the same interface on the"
" server and on the client. A WebSocket driver is an object with two "
"duplex streams attached; one for incoming/outgoing messages and one for "
"managing the wire protocol over an I/O stream. The full API is described "
"below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:49
msgid "Server-side with HTTP"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:51
msgid ""
"A Node webserver emits a special event for 'upgrade' requests, and this "
"is where you should handle WebSockets. You first check whether the "
"request is a WebSocket, and if so you can create a driver and attach the "
"request's I/O stream to it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:78
msgid ""
"Note the line `driver.io.write(body)` - you must pass the `body` buffer "
"to the socket driver in order to make certain versions of the protocol "
"work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:82
msgid "Server-side with TCP"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:84
msgid ""
"You can also handle WebSocket connections in a bare TCP server, if you're"
" not using an HTTP server and don't want to implement HTTP parsing "
"yourself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:87
msgid ""
"The driver will emit a `connect` event when a request is received, and at"
" this point you can detect whether it's a WebSocket and handle it as "
"such. Here's an example using the Node `net` module:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:117
msgid ""
"In the `connect` event, the driver gains several properties to describe "
"the request, similar to a Node request object, such as `method`, `url` "
"and `headers`. However you should remember it's not a real request "
"object; you cannot write data to it, it only tells you what request data "
"we parsed from the input."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:123
msgid ""
"If the request has a body, it will be in the `driver.body` buffer, but "
"only as much of the body as has been piped into the driver when the "
"`connect` event fires."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:128
msgid "Client-side"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:130
msgid ""
"Similarly, to implement a WebSocket client you just need to make a driver"
" by passing in a URL. After this you use the driver API as described "
"below to process incoming data and send outgoing data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:153
msgid ""
"Client drivers have two additional properties for reading the HTTP data "
"that was sent back by the server:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:156
msgid "`driver.statusCode` - the integer value of the HTTP status code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:157
msgid "`driver.headers` - an object containing the response headers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:160
msgid "HTTP Proxies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:162
msgid ""
"The client driver supports connections via HTTP proxies using the "
"`CONNECT` method. Instead of sending the WebSocket handshake immediately,"
" it will send a `CONNECT` request, wait for a `200` response, and then "
"proceed as normal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:166
msgid ""
"To use this feature, call `driver.proxy(url)` where `url` is the origin "
"of the proxy, including a username and password if required. This "
"produces a duplex stream that you should pipe in and out of your TCP "
"connection to the proxy server. When the proxy emits `connect`, you can "
"then pipe `driver.io` to your TCP stream and call `driver.start()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:196
msgid ""
"The proxy's `connect` event is also where you should perform a TLS "
"handshake on your TCP stream, if you are connecting to a `wss:` endpoint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:199
msgid ""
"In the event that proxy connection fails, `proxy` will emit an `error`. "
"You can inspect the proxy's response via `proxy.statusCode` and "
"`proxy.headers`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:210
msgid ""
"Before calling `proxy.start()` you can set custom headers using "
"`proxy.setHeader()`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:219
msgid "Driver API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:221
msgid "Drivers are created using one of the following methods:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:229
msgid ""
"The `http` method returns a driver chosen using the headers from a Node "
"HTTP request object. The `server` method returns a driver that will parse"
" an HTTP request and then decide which driver to use for it using the "
"`http` method. The `client` method always returns a driver for the RFC "
"version of the protocol with masking enabled on outgoing frames."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:235
msgid ""
"The `options` argument is optional, and is an object. It may contain the "
"following fields:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:238
msgid ""
"`maxLength` - the maximum allowed size of incoming message frames, in "
"bytes. The default value is `2^26 - 1`, or 1 byte short of 64 MiB."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:240
msgid ""
"`protocols` - an array of strings representing acceptable subprotocols "
"for use over the socket. The driver will negotiate one of these to use "
"via the `Sec-WebSocket-Protocol` header if supported by the other peer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:244
msgid "A driver has two duplex streams attached to it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:246
msgid ""
"**`driver.io`** - this stream should be attached to an I/O socket like a "
"TCP stream. Pipe incoming TCP chunks to this stream for them to be "
"parsed, and pipe this stream back into TCP to send outgoing frames."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:249
msgid ""
"**`driver.messages`** - this stream emits messages received over the "
"WebSocket.  Writing to it sends messages to the other peer by emitting "
"frames via the `driver.io` stream."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:253
msgid ""
"All drivers respond to the following API methods, but some of them are "
"no-ops depending on whether the client supports the behaviour."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:256
msgid ""
"Note that most of these methods are commands: if they produce data that "
"should be sent over the socket, they will give this to you by emitting "
"`data` events on the `driver.io` stream."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:260
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`driver.on('open', function(event) {})`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:262
msgid "Adds a callback to execute when the socket becomes open."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:264
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`driver.on('message', function(event) {})`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:266
msgid ""
"Adds a callback to execute when a message is received. `event` will have "
"a `data` attribute containing either a string in the case of a text "
"message or a `Buffer` in the case of a binary message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:270
msgid ""
"You can also listen for messages using the `driver.messages.on('data')` "
"event, which emits strings for text messages and buffers for binary "
"messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:273
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`driver.on('error', function(event) {})`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:275
msgid ""
"Adds a callback to execute when a protocol error occurs due to the other "
"peer sending an invalid byte sequence. `event` will have a `message` "
"attribute describing the error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:279
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`driver.on('close', function(event) {})`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:281
msgid ""
"Adds a callback to execute when the socket becomes closed. The `event` "
"object has `code` and `reason` attributes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:284
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`driver.on('ping', function(event) {})`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:286
msgid ""
"Adds a callback block to execute when a ping is received. You do not need"
" to handle this by sending a pong frame yourself; the driver handles this"
" for you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:289
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`driver.on('pong', function(event) {})`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:291
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Adds a callback block to execute when a pong is received. If this was in "
"response to a ping you sent, you can also handle this event via the "
"`driver.ping(message, function() { ... })` callback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:295
msgid "`driver.addExtension(extension)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:297
msgid ""
"Registers a protocol extension whose operation will be negotiated via the"
" `Sec-WebSocket-Extensions` header. `extension` is any extension "
"compatible with the [websocket-extensions](https://github.com/faye"
"/websocket-extensions-node) framework."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:302
msgid "`driver.setHeader(name, value)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:304
msgid ""
"Sets a custom header to be sent as part of the handshake response, either"
" from the server or from the client. Must be called before `start()`, "
"since this is when the headers are serialized and sent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:308
msgid "`driver.start()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:310
msgid ""
"Initiates the protocol by sending the handshake - either the response for"
" a server-side driver or the request for a client-side one. This should "
"be the first method you invoke.  Returns `true` if and only if a "
"handshake was sent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:314
msgid "`driver.parse(string)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:316
msgid ""
"Takes a string and parses it, potentially resulting in message events "
"being emitted (see `on('message')` above) or in data being sent to "
"`driver.io`.  You should send all data you receive via I/O to this method"
" by piping a stream into `driver.io`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:321
msgid "`driver.text(string)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:323
msgid ""
"Sends a text message over the socket. If the socket handshake is not yet "
"complete, the message will be queued until it is. Returns `true` if the "
"message was sent or queued, and `false` if the socket can no longer send "
"messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:327
msgid "This method is equivalent to `driver.messages.write(string)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:329
msgid "`driver.binary(buffer)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:331
msgid ""
"Takes a `Buffer` and sends it as a binary message. Will queue and return "
"`true` or `false` the same way as the `text` method. It will also return "
"`false` if the driver does not support binary messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:335
msgid "This method is equivalent to `driver.messages.write(buffer)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:337
#, python-brace-format
msgid "`driver.ping(string = '', function() {})`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:339
msgid ""
"Sends a ping frame over the socket, queueing it if necessary. `string` "
"and the callback are both optional. If a callback is given, it will be "
"invoked when the socket receives a pong frame whose content matches "
"`string`. Returns `false` if frames can no longer be sent, or if the "
"driver does not support ping/pong."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:344
msgid "`driver.pong(string = '')`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:346
msgid ""
"Sends a pong frame over the socket, queueing it if necessary. `string` is"
" optional. Returns `false` if frames can no longer be sent, or if the "
"driver does not support ping/pong."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:350
msgid ""
"You don't need to call this when a ping frame is received; pings are "
"replied to automatically by the driver. This method is for sending "
"unsolicited pongs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:353
msgid "`driver.close()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:355
msgid ""
"Initiates the closing handshake if the socket is still open. For drivers "
"with no closing handshake, this will result in the immediate execution of"
" the `on('close')` driver. For drivers with a closing handshake, this "
"sends a closing frame and `emit('close')` will execute when a response is"
" received or a protocol error occurs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:361
msgid "`driver.version`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:363
msgid ""
"Returns the WebSocket version in use as a string. Will either be "
"`hixie-75`, `hixie-76` or `hybi-$version`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:366
msgid "`driver.protocol`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/websocket-driver_README.md:368
msgid ""
"Returns a string containing the selected subprotocol, if any was agreed "
"upon using the `Sec-WebSocket-Protocol` mechanism. This value becomes "
"available after `emit('open')` has fired."
msgstr ""

